# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop() inside a try/finally block runs the finally clause
#         before unwinding the tag scope; finally body executes exactly once.
#
# defer-to: T29
#
# Reason: requires UTag runtime + TAG_STOP absorption in the unwind walker
# (T29).  Additionally, the interaction between TAG_STOP propagation and
# TRY_FRAME finally execution is gated on T30 (OP_PUSH_TAG runtime extension)
# since the walker must handle the combined CALL_FRAME / TRY_FRAME / TAG_SCOPE
# stack ordering correctly.
#
# When T29/T30 land, implement this fixture by uncommenting the source below.
# Expected behaviour: finally body runs ("cleanup") then tag scope exits.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T29/T30):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   var cleaned = 0;
#   t: { try { t.stop() } finally { cleaned = 1 } };
#   cleaned
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 1
